From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/mov: group a Dolby Vision enhancement track in an
 HEVC sample entry

The dual-track Dolby Vision carriage of MP4 (Annex C of "Dolby Vision
Streams Within the ISO Base Media File Format") puts the enhancement layer
of a profile 7 stream in a track of its own, with a 'vdep' reference to the
base track and a 'dvcC' record. mov_parse_dovi_streams() only grouped such
a track when its sample entry was 'dvhe' or 'dvh1'. Some muxers write the
enhancement track with an ordinary HEVC sample entry, 'hvc1' or 'hev1',
with the same record in it. No group was made for those files, so the
player saw two unrelated HEVC tracks and played the base layer alone, as
HDR10.

Take such a track too, with a stricter rule than for the Dolby Vision
sample entries, because an ordinary HEVC entry says nothing about Dolby
Vision by itself: its record must be the one of a profile 7 enhancement
layer with its RPU and without a base layer (as for every entry), and its
'vdep' reference must name exactly one track. mov_read_vdep() keeps the
first track of a box and warns about the others, as before; it now also
counts how many tracks the references name (up to 2), so that a
reference to several tracks is not taken for one.

Nothing changes for the 'dvhe' and 'dvh1' entries, nor for any track
whose record is not the one of a profile 7 enhancement layer.

The idea is from the CroqueMr fork (ffmpeg-9900-07); written anew.
---
 libavformat/isom.h |  1 +
 libavformat/mov.c  | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/isom.h b/libavformat/isom.h
--- a/libavformat/isom.h
+++ b/libavformat/isom.h
@@ -95,6 +95,7 @@ typedef struct MovTref {
     uint32_t    name;
     int         nb_id;
     uint32_t   *id; ///< trackID of the referenced track
+    int         nb_declared; ///< 'vdep': tracks the boxes name, up to 2 (the reader keeps the first of each)
 } MovTref;
 
 typedef struct MOVAtom {
diff --git a/libavformat/mov.c b/libavformat/mov.c
--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -2681,6 +2681,10 @@ static int mov_read_vdep(MOVContext* c, AVIOContext* pb, MOVAtom atom)
     if (ret < 0)
         return ret;
 
+    /* how many tracks the references name, so that a reference to one track
+     * can be told from one to several (mov_parse_dovi_streams) */
+    tag->nb_declared = FFMIN(tag->nb_declared + (atom.size > 4 ? 2 : 1), 2);
+
     return 0;
 }
 
@@ -11228,7 +11232,12 @@ static int mov_parse_dovi_streams(AVFormatContext *s)
      * v2.7.1. The 'vdep' track reference type is shared with depth video
      * and multi-view dependencies. The spec-mandated DV-specific sample
      * entry combined with the dvcC configuration record disambiguates
-     * those uses. */
+     * those uses.
+     * Some muxers write the enhancement track with an ordinary HEVC sample
+     * entry ('hvc1' or 'hev1') that carries the same configuration record.
+     * Such a track is taken too, with a stricter rule than the DV-specific
+     * entries: its record must be the one of a profile 7 enhancement layer
+     * (below) and its 'vdep' reference must name one track and no other. */
     for (int i = 0; i < s->nb_streams; i++) {
         AVStreamGroup *stg;
         AVStream *st = s->streams[i];
@@ -11237,12 +11246,15 @@ static int mov_parse_dovi_streams(AVFormatContext *s)
         MovTref *tag = mov_find_tref_tag(sc, MKTAG('v','d','e','p'));
         const AVPacketSideData *sd;
         const AVDOVIDecoderConfigurationRecord *dovi;
+        int hevc_entry;
 
         if (st->codecpar->codec_id != AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC || !tag)
             continue;
 
+        hevc_entry = st->codecpar->codec_tag == MKTAG('h','v','c','1') ||
+                     st->codecpar->codec_tag == MKTAG('h','e','v','1');
         if (st->codecpar->codec_tag != MKTAG('d','v','h','e') &&
-            st->codecpar->codec_tag != MKTAG('d','v','h','1'))
+            st->codecpar->codec_tag != MKTAG('d','v','h','1') && !hevc_entry)
             continue;
 
         sd = av_packet_side_data_get(st->codecpar->coded_side_data,
@@ -11258,6 +11270,13 @@ static int mov_parse_dovi_streams(AVFormatContext *s)
             !dovi->el_present_flag || dovi->bl_present_flag)
             continue;
 
+        if (hevc_entry && (tag->nb_id != 1 || tag->nb_declared != 1)) {
+            av_log(s, AV_LOG_WARNING, "Dolby Vision EL stream in an HEVC sample "
+                   "entry with a 'vdep' reference to more than one track: not "
+                   "grouped\n");
+            continue;
+        }
+
         st_base = mov_find_reference_track(s, st, tag->id, tag->nb_id, 0);
         if (!st_base) {
             int loglevel = (s->error_recognition & AV_EF_EXPLODE) ? AV_LOG_ERROR : AV_LOG_WARNING;
-- 
2.53.0

